In the following decades, there were more moving sidewalk proposals in cities throughout Europe. And then, in 1893 at the Chicago World's Fair, they actually built one out on a pier into Lake Michigan. And you paid a fee and you could ride out on the moving sidewalk, out at the end of the pier, see the lake, and it would curve around, and it would bring you back. So instead of transportation system, it was kind of an amusement ride, sort of. But it was the 1900 World's Fair in Paris, where Spears' idea was most fully realized. A pretty amazing technological feat for the time, so it was about four kilometers long, a full circle, in the city of Paris, pretty much in the center.
在接下来的几十年里，欧洲各地的城市出现了更多的移动人行道提案。然后，在1893年的芝加哥世博会上，他们真的在伸入密歇根湖的码头上建造了一条。你付了钱就可以坐上移动人行道，一直到码头尽头，看看湖景，它会转弯，然后把你带回来。所以与其说它是交通系统，不如说它是一种游乐设施。但正是在1900年的巴黎世博会上，斯皮尔的想法得到了最充分的实现。这对当时来说是一项相当了不起的技术成就，它全长约四公里，在巴黎市中心绕了一个完整的圆圈。

