Of the course of about 25 minutes, the walkway would carry passengers through the city center traversing the footprint of the fair. This was not an amusement park ride relegated to a pier. It was in your face. At certain points, quite literally. In some places, the Dirtua Ruland ran along boulevards, and because it was on a higher level on a platform, so it ended up being in front of people's windows.
在大约25分钟的时间里，人行道载着乘客穿过市中心，横跨整个博览会的占地范围。这不再是一个被降级到码头的游乐园设施。它就在你面前。在某些地方，简直是近在咫尺。在某些路段，“Trottoir Roulant”沿着林荫大道运行，因为它位于较高的平台上，所以最终出现在人们的窗前。

