running continuously for several months. Some of the earliest surviving silent film is of people riding the Paris moving walkway. Thomas Edison's film company was actually there documenting the whole thing. They placed a camera on the walkway and let it roll. Watching the film, you see this mass of wood and electricity gliding through central Paris. You see the ornate apartments and grand festival buildings go by. And you can really imagine the sheer thrill it would have been to take this ride.
连续运行了几个月。一些现存最早的无声电影就是人们乘坐巴黎移动人行道的画面。托马斯·爱迪生的电影公司当时就在现场记录这一切。他们把摄像机放在人行道上，让它转动。看着电影，你会看到这团木头和电力在巴黎市中心滑行。你看到华丽的公寓和宏伟的节日建筑掠过。你真的可以想象乘坐这种交通工具会是多么令人兴奋。

